{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, לָהֵן²","hw":"לָהֵן²","html":"† II. <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">לָהֵן</span></big></big>  <strong>conj. except, but (</strong>from <span dir=\"rtl\">לָא</span> and <span dir=\"rtl\">הֵן</span> ‘not if’ (cf. Heb. <a data-ref=\"BDB Aramaic, לָא\" href=\"/BDB Aramaic,_לָא\", dir=\"rtl\">אם לא</a> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:38\" href=\"/Genesis.24.38\">Gn 24:38</a>); so Nab. and Egyptian Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">להן</span> Cooke<sup>217, 219, 241</sup> S-C<sup>Pap. C 6, 7 +</sup>; <em>lâinnî</em>, <em>however</em> Socin<sup>Arabic Dial. v. Marokko 44, Anm. 103</sup>; 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">אִילָּהֵין</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 32:28\" href=\"/Genesis.32.28\">Gn 32:28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 43:3\" href=\"/Genesis.43.3\">43:3</a> al.<strong>)</strong>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  after a neg. (= BH <span dir=\"rtl\">כִּי אִם</span>, q.v.): <strong>a.</strong>  <em>except</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:11\" href=\"/Daniel.2.11\">Dn 2:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:28\" href=\"/Daniel.3.28\">3:28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:6\" href=\"/Daniel.6.6\">6:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:8\" href=\"/Daniel.6.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:13\" href=\"/Daniel.6.13\">13</a>. <strong>b.</strong>  <em>but</em> (Germ. <em>sondern</em>) <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:30\" href=\"/Daniel.2.30\">Dn 2:30</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  without a neg.: <em>however, but</em> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 5:12\" href=\"/Ezra.5.12\">Ezr 5:12</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, לֵוָי","prev":"BDB Aramaic, לָהֵן"}